# Line endings are normalised in the index, not left to each machine's
# core.autocrlf. Every blob in this repo is already LF, so this changes no content —
# it stops a future clone from committing CRLF into a *generated and byte-compared*
# artifact. NodeDocsExportTest and NodeStringsSyncTest normalise CRLF before
# comparing and would survive, but the website's tokens.css drift guard is a raw
# `git diff --exit-code` and would not, and CRLF in `gradlew` breaks it on Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one thing that genuinely wants CRLF in the working
# tree. The index copy stays LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# `gradlew` is a shell script executed by the CI runner. Never CRLF.
gradlew text eol=lf

*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary
